### The Problem with Custom Error Middleware

For years, ASP.NET Core developers relied on custom exception-handling middleware wrapped in `try-catch` blocks to standardize API error responses. While functional, this approach often clutters the request pipeline, muddies logging scopes, and duplicates status-code mapping logic across services.

### The Built-in Solution: IExceptionHandler

ASP.NET Core 8 introduced the `IExceptionHandler` interface, offering a standardized, first-class contract for processing unhandled exceptions globally. Instead of managing raw delegate chains, you implement this interface, return a boolean indicating if the exception was handled, and map errors to RFC 7807 problem details cleanly.

### Before

```csharp
public class CustomMiddleware
{
    private readonly RequestDelegate _next;
    public CustomMiddleware(RequestDelegate next) => _next = next;

    public async Task Invoke(HttpContext ctx)
    {
        try { await _next(ctx); }
        catch (Exception ex) { /* messy handling */ }
    }
}
```

### After

```csharp
public class GlobalHandler : IExceptionHandler
{
    public async ValueTask<bool> TryHandleAsync(
        HttpContext ctx, Exception ex, CancellationToken ct)
    {
        if (ex is not NotFoundException) return false;
        ctx.Response.StatusCode = StatusCodes.Status404NotFound;
        await ctx.Response.WriteAsJsonAsync(new { error = ex.Message }, ct);
        return true;
    }
}
```

### Why It Matters

* **Pipeline Integration:** Native framework support cleanly intercepts errors without manual delegate wrapping.
* **Status Mapping:** Centralized logic maps domain exceptions directly to appropriate HTTP response codes.
* **Memory Efficiency:** Avoids excessive heap allocations during exception execution paths.

### Watch Out

Make sure to register your implementation via `services.AddExceptionHandler<GlobalHandler>()` and add `app.UseExceptionHandler()` early in your middleware pipeline, or unhandled faults will still fall through to the default developer exception page.

